    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d850">

                <pb facs="0788" n="672" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg672"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 882.51/313C.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Special Representative of Dr.
                    Falkner</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 27, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to yesterday’s cable,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d850-f1"/> Liberian
                    Government is probably about to default on interest on 1871 loan due April 1. If
                    this should occur it will change the situation as regards negotiations with
                    bondholders. Have cabled Monrovia for explanation; until this is received you
                    will await in London further instructions from Department. In Department’s
                    opinion this situation means merely slight delay and need not interfere with the
                    plans of General Receiver Clark.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
